{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/436789-spoilers-inspiration-for-how-the-deceived-see-their-connection-to-seba","id":436789,"title":"[Spoilers?] Inspiration for how the Deceived see their connection to Seba","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T00:27:11-07:00","id":436789,"title":"[Spoilers?] Inspiration for how the Deceived see their connection to Seba","content":"I came across the link below during a course at university and I think it has some interesting ideas on the creative process. In particular at about 10 minutes into it, (after the somewhat less useful talk of daemons &amp; geniuses/fairies) it describes the process as a supernatural force that moves through the world and once 'caught' is represented as art, (in this case poetry).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/elizabeth_gilbert_on_genius\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pi.tedcdn.com/r/pe.tedcdn.com/images/ted/f2f6d094758c36a61b3ee7992a9b197eb4c07979_2880x1620.jpg?u%5Br%5D=2&amp;u%5Bs%5D=0.5&amp;u%5Ba%5D=0.8&amp;u%5Bt%5D=0.03&amp;quality=80&amp;c=1050%2C550&amp;w=1050\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/elizabeth_gilbert_on_genius\" target=\"_blank\"> Your elusive creative genius </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/elizabeth_gilbert_on_genius\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ted.com/talks/elizabeth_gilbert_on_genius </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Elizabeth Gilbert muses on the impossible things we expect from artists and geniuses -- and shares the radical idea that, instead of the rare person \"being\" a genius, all of us \"have\" a genius. It's a funny, personal and surprisingly moving talk. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought it might be worth sharing. I also wonder if the Devs have ever felt anything similar during their careers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:33:39-07:00","id":437540,"title":"","content":"Inspiration like a palpable lightning bolt searing its way into my brain with a sudden flash of inspiration that would otherwise take me days or longer to work out? Yeah, you just described what it's like when I'm in the manic phase of my bipolar. That's why the Poet works the way it does; it's a bit of autobiography of my personal madness. Thankfully, my current meds keep the mania away so that hasn't happened since last summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}